// Scavenging: the player searches for supplies at a fast-travel place.
// The engine runs the search (a perception roll against `target`); these are its
// texts and numbers. `generic` is the event found most of the time; other events
// "found by: scavenging in <zone>" come up the rest of the time.

== scavenge_rules woodland_scavenging
generic: forage
generic chance: 2 in 3
target: 8
start: You set out to forage along the edges of the woods.
found: [one of]Following a deer trail, you come across[or]Poking under the ferns, you find[at random]
failure: You come back empty-handed.
only at: You can only forage from places you know well (fast travel points).

// The generic find. It must be found by scavenging; the rule picks it most of the time.
== event forage
name: A little forage
found by: scavenging in forest
repeat: always
play:
    [one of]A bramble heavy with berries.[or]A patch of berries under the ferns.[or]Berries, a little squashed but sweet.[at random]
    ~ give wild_berries
